20.8  jq

TL;DR
  - jq filters JSON: give it a path, get the value back.
  - . is the whole input, pretty-printed. .name is a field, .items[] each
    element of an array, and | chains filters.
  - -r prints strings without quotes, ready for the shell.

      curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/jqlang/jq | jq .stargazers_count
      jq -r '.dependencies | keys[]' package.json
      jq '.[] | select(.age > 30) | .name' people.json

Pitfalls
  - Usually not installed by default: the package is jq on every major distro.
  - Put the filter in single quotes: [], | and $ mean something to the shell.
  - A missing field gives null, not an error. .port // 8080 gives a default
    instead.
  - jq can't edit a file in place: write to a temporary file, then move it over
    the original.

Deep dive: 2 questions. Read them with idk 20.8 --why

Related
